  "schemaVersion": "1.0",
  "scriptId": "avg-04-combined-groups-and-group-ratios",
  "sourceType": "MANUAL",
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Combined Groups and Group Ratios",
    "description": "Combine group means and work backward to find an unknown group mean, size, ratio or percentage.",
    "teachingApproach": "Start by physically rebuilding two group totals, then reverse the process to find an unknown group mean or size. From that equation derive the opposite-gap/alligation ratio, convert ratios to counts and percentages, apply it to passed/failed groups, and finish with a three-group capstone that requires finding an intermediate ratio first.",
    "targetDurationMinutes": 32,
    "sourceScope": "Teach combined averages by converting each subgroup mean to a subgroup total. Work backward to find an unknown subgroup mean or subgroup size. Then derive the two-group balance/alligation idea: the combined mean lies between the two group means, and the group-size ratio is obtained from the opposite gaps. Use this to find ratios, percentages and passed/failed or boys/girls counts. Finish with a three-group capstone where one combined mean first reveals an internal ratio."
  },
  "startNodeId": "start",
  "nodes": {
    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's learn how two different group averages combine.\n\nThe key question is never 'What is the average of the two averages?' It is 'How much total does each group contribute, and how many people contributed it?'",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1": {
      "id": "teach_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Two groups can be merged only after we rebuild their totals.\n\nTwenty people average 50, so their total is 1000. Thirty people average 70, so their total is 2100.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1_step": {
      "id": "teach_1_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Combined total = 3100\nCombined count = 50\nCombined average = 3100 ÷ 50 = 62\n\nNotice how the larger 70-group pulls the answer above 60.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "q_1": {
